Takeoff is a Hard Linux machine built around a realistic airline-booking application called HTB Airways Booking. The application allows users to register accounts, search for flights, select seats, purchase tickets, download boarding passes, and check in using QR codes.
The external attack surface appeared small because only SSH and HTTP were exposed. However, the web application contained several vulnerabilities that could be combined into a complete attack chain.

The overall attack path was:  Web enumeration
→ Account registration
→ Flight booking
→ PDF ticket SSTI
→ Environment secret disclosure
→ Signed QR ticket reconstruction
→ Command execution as www-data
→ Internal n8n API access
→ Container command execution as root
→ Access to kpark’s mounted home directory
→ SSH access as kpark
→ Setuid Bash privilege escalation
→ Root access

